enomenon known as the <b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"159"=
>highly conductive blood film</b>. This thin layer of fluid trapped between=
 the electrode surface and the solid tissue acts as a significant electrica=
l and physical barrier, directly altering the sensed impedance data.</p><p =
data-path-to-node=3D"1">Understanding how this film behaves at the microsco=
pic level dictates how your sensing algorithms must interpret the data to a=
ccurately classify tissue.</p><h2 data-path-to-node=3D"3">1. The Physics of=
 the "Blood Shunt" Effect</h2><p data-path-to-node=3D"4">Blood is an except=
ionally good conductor of electricity, with a conductivity (<span class=3D"=
math-inline" data-math=3D"\sigma" data-index-in-node=3D"78"><span class=3D"=
katex"><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"=
><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class=3D"mo=
rd mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.0359em;">=CF=83</span></span></span=
></span></span>) of roughly <span class=3D"math-inline" data-math=3D"0.7 \t=
ext{ S/m}" data-index-in-node=3D"97"><span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"k=
atex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" =
style=3D"height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord"=
>0.7</span><span class=3D"mord text"><span class=3D"mord">&nbsp;S/m</span><=
/span></span></span></span></span> at body temperature, driven primarily by=
 dissolved electrolytes in the plasma. In contrast, an organizing embolic c=
lot or the arterial wall tissue is significantly more resistive.</p><p data=
-path-to-node=3D"5">When a flat electrode comes into close proximity with a=
 clot, a microscopic film of blood remains trapped in the interface. Becaus=
e electricity naturally follows the path of least resistance, the injected =
current will preferentially pass laterally through this highly conductive b=
lood film rather than penetrating deeply into the clot or vessel wall.</p><=
ul data-path-to-node=3D"6"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"6,0,0"><b data-path-=
to-node=3D"6,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The Measurement Error:</b> This =
"shunting" effect masks the true electrical signature of the target. The sy=
stem registers a very low impedance (characteristic of pure blood), complet=
ely missing the higher resistance and unique capacitive phase angle (<span =
class=3D"math-inline" data-math=3D"\theta" data-index-in-node=3D"247"><span=
