d impedance drops; during diastole (low flow), it rises. This creates a rhy=
thmic artifact tied to the patient's heartbeat.</p></li><li><p data-path-to=
-node=3D"5,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"5,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Tem=
perature:</b> Blood conductivity changes by roughly <b data-path-to-node=3D=
"5,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"51">2% per degree Celsius</b>. A fever or loc=
